Subject: SAIL Ontology Inference Import Formation

& [SpecificationIdentity] is the canonical SJS formation specification
  + [specification_uuid] is de1c3931-f3e4-4eb2-ac89-a5cebe4c27c4
  + [status] is formation_not_implementation_authority
  + [purpose] is preserve external ontology semantics while projecting useful structures into SAIL

& [StandardsValueBeyondCurrentSOP] is the interest supplied by mature ontology systems
  + [formal_model_theory] is mathematically specified meaning independent of one interpreter prompt
  + [entailment_regimes] is named and testable inference behavior
  + [world_assumptions] is explicit open-world and monotonic reasoning behavior
  + [property_algebra] is transitive, symmetric, asymmetric, inverse, functional, inverse-functional, and chained relations
  + [class_expression] is intersection, union, complement, enumeration, existential restriction, universal restriction, and qualified cardinality
  + [identity_semantics] is explicit same, different, key, mapping, and disjointness relations
  + [validation_shape] is reusable path, cardinality, datatype, closed-shape, severity, and report structures
  + [concept_governance] is preferred, alternate, hidden, broader, narrower, related, exact-match, and close-match semantics
  + [provenance_qualification] is derivation, attribution, delegation, generation, use, activity, agent, bundle, and qualified relation structure
  + [interoperability_ecosystem] is existing vocabularies, reasoners, validators, query engines, serializers, and datasets
  = conclusion: SOP may express these forms, but flexibility alone does not establish their exact laws, compatibility, decidability, tests, or ecosystem

& [ImportSemanticBoundary] is the rule against naive direct conversion
  + [external_ontology] contains assertions, axioms, shapes, vocabulary declarations, and annotations rather than ordinary executable instructions
  + [SAIL_program] contains attention operations, inference requests, effects, authority, faults, and termination
  = must: not reinterpret every ontology statement as an executable SOP directive
  = must: preserve the source language, source graph, ontology identifier, version, digest, namespace, entailment regime, and world assumption
  = must: distinguish asserted statements from imported entailments and SAIL-generated interpretations
  = must: reject or quarantine constructs with no semantics-preserving SAIL representation

& [InferenceImportPipeline] is the staged ontology-to-SAIL process
  + [stage_1_preserve] is store immutable source bytes, media type, locator, digest, ontology and version identifiers, and import closure
  + [stage_2_parse] is parse RDF syntax into a syntax-neutral external graph
  + [stage_3_classify] is identify vocabulary declarations, assertions, axioms, shapes, annotations, provenance, and unsupported constructs
  + [stage_4_reason] is optionally compute entailments under an explicitly selected bounded regime
  + [stage_5_map] is apply versioned declarative mappings into the SAIL semantic intermediate representation
  + [stage_6_validate] is validate the mapped representation and emit losses, collisions, contradictions, and confidence
  + [stage_7_project] is generate human-readable SOP views and library candidates
  + [stage_8_admit] is require governance review before a candidate becomes authoritative SAIL library content
  = must: make the import repeatable and deterministic for the same source, mapping version, and reasoner version

& [ImportRecord] is the inspectable import identity
  + [import_uuid] is stable import-event identity
  + [source_digest] is immutable external content identity
  + [source_semantics] is RDF, RDFS, OWL profile, SHACL, SKOS, PROV-O, schema.org, or another declared regime
  + [mapping_profile_uuid] is the exact translation policy
  + [reasoner_identity] is engine, version, profile, and configuration
  + [asserted_graph] is unmodified source assertions
  + [entailed_graph] is derived claims separated from assertions
  + [SAIL_projection] is generated SAIL IR and readable SOP view
  + [loss_report] is unsupported or weakened semantics
  + [conflict_report] is collisions, inconsistencies, validation faults, and contextual incompatibilities
  + [authority_state] is quarantined, candidate, reviewed, admitted, superseded, or rejected

& [ConversionClasses] is the translation fidelity declaration
  + [isomorphic] is reversible without semantic loss
  + [equivalent_profile] is meaning-preserving inside a declared restricted profile
  + [sound_approximation] is every imported inference remains justified but some source inferences may be unavailable
  + [descriptive_projection] is useful for search or explanation but not equivalent authority
  + [unsupported] is preserved without reinterpretation
  = must: label every mapping with one conversion class

& [LibraryAdmissionBoundary] is protection of the SOP library
  + [imported_source_library] is preserved external ontology material and mappings
  + [generated_candidate_library] is machine-produced SOP projections awaiting review
  + [canonical_SAIL_library] is reviewed and signed native authority
  = must: not allow inference import to write directly into canonical SAIL authority
  = must: maintain links from every admitted element to assertion, entailment, mapping rule, source, and review decision

& [RequirementSet] is the traceable formation requirement collection
  + [IMP-001] is preserve external ontology semantics and provenance before interpretation
  + [IMP-002] is separate assertions, entailments, and SAIL interpretations
  + [IMP-003] is translate through a versioned semantic IR mapping rather than prose-only model inference
  + [IMP-004] is declare conversion fidelity and semantic losses
  + [IMP-005] is quarantine unsupported or conflicting constructs
  + [IMP-006] is admit generated SOP library content only through governed review
  + [IMP-007] is make imports repeatable under pinned parser, reasoner, mapping, and source versions

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is the ontology inference import trace
  + [fold_1_subject] is standards-derived semantic structures imported into SAIL
  + [fold_2_boundary] is external assertions and entailments preserved outside canonical SAIL authority
  + [fold_3_data_design] is source, graph, regime, mapping, reasoner, projection, loss, conflict, and admission identities
  + [fold_4_governance] is generated projections remain candidates until reviewed and signed
  + [fold_5_solution_shape] is preserve, parse, classify, reason, map, validate, project, and admit
  + [fold_6_fault_review] is semantic drift, execution confusion, assertion-entailment collapse, prompt nondeterminism, unsupported constructs, and authority contamination
  + [fold_7_phase_lock] is import semantics formed; parser and mapping implementation await representative-corpus proof

